WEBVTT

00:00:02.830 --> 00:00:11.910
Long, long ago, before Tanda ever had wings, she was a shipbuilder's daughter, at the edge of a cold grey sea.

00:00:11.910 --> 00:00:19.910
Her father built ships that could cross the world. But he taught her something far harder... how to notice.

00:00:19.910 --> 00:00:25.530
And the night her very first tooth came loose... everything began to change.

00:00:25.530 --> 00:00:35.910
He set a bright coin beside it. A tooth fee, he said. Not a purchase. A promise to notice.

00:00:35.910 --> 00:00:43.630
When the ship sailed, he carried her tooth on a cord, close to his heart. Until I come home.

00:00:43.630 --> 00:00:48.450
And the sea... took him away.

00:00:48.450 --> 00:00:53.570
Across the water waited fog, and hunger, and a long, hard winter.

00:00:53.570 --> 00:01:01.770
Then, one morning, they found a boy. A thief, they said... clutching a stolen rope.

00:01:01.770 --> 00:01:07.570
Her father was big enough to frighten him. Tired enough to want to.

00:01:07.570 --> 00:01:16.690
But the little tooth tapped against his chest. And he remembered her hands closing around it. Still mine.

00:01:16.690 --> 00:01:25.450
The rope was no treasure. It was all that held a broken boat together... for a boy, and his barefoot sister.

00:01:25.450 --> 00:01:33.370
So he chose kindness. Tools, not shouting. Trading, not taking.

00:01:33.370 --> 00:01:39.690
And that night, the tooth began to glow. The very first Toothlight.

00:01:39.690 --> 00:01:44.890
When the ship came home, she ran before she remembered she had legs.

00:01:44.890 --> 00:01:51.010
It remembers, she whispered. You remembered first, he said.

00:01:51.010 --> 00:01:56.650
And so, light gathered around her shoulders... and the promise grew wings.

00:01:56.650 --> 00:02:03.530
Tanda became the very first Tooth Fairy. And somewhere, another child was letting go of something small.
